    dogfood: auger PROMISING-BUT-ROUGH (5th run) — a REAL drill judged as a product: the loop produces a genuinely useful configuration, but `answer` reports success over a configuration that selects NOTHING, and the ask gate re-proposes the question it just closed
    
    Fifth dogfood run, and the first to change the ANGLE rather than repeat the entry
    surface. Runs 1-4 proved the machinery (core loop; graph/bundles/verdict;
    ask->answer seam + registers; raw HTTP layer). Every one asked "does the verb
    work". This run asked the user's question: does drilling a REAL decision set
    produce something worth reading?
    
    The drill: a real fleet decision (where heavy multiarch docker builds run, forced
    by the 2026-08-31 rethinkdb qemu incident), real alternatives, real rejected
    reasons. Empty namespace -> rendered configuration in ~90s.
    
    Findings (rows AUG-055..AUG-060):
    
    - AUG-055 (P1) `answer` sets option.active by a byte-for-byte `--chosen ==
      --option` comparison (auger.py cmd_answer). A chosen short name vs a full-sentence
      option stores ZERO active options, prints "D-001 recorded" and exits 0; only
      `dump` reveals "ACTIVE CONFIGURATION: (nothing active)". It also makes
      `dump --config` print a spurious CONTRADICTIONS WITH THE RECORD line.
    - AUG-056 (P1) the already-answered gate scores similarity, not identity: after
      `answer --question-id Q-000001` closed Q-000001, the next `ask` stored Q-000002
      with the IDENTICAL text, costing a duplicate decision before JEV said "nothing
      left worth asking".
    - AUG-057 (P2) `--why-not` does not repeat while `--option` does — a second
      reason is silently dropped at exit 0.
    - AUG-058 (P2) `option.costs`/`option.breaks` are declared and rendered but no
      verb can ever set them; `dump` prints `costs=— breaks=—` forever.
    - AUG-059 (P2) `status` self-contradicts: a domain leads with "answered" and ends
      "(row status NOT-REACHED)".
    - AUG-060 (P2) the documented fixed substrate port is unsafe on a shared host: on
      the CI box a fresh agent got a 500 whose message named a DESTROYED agent's home,
      answered by another owner's/orphaned daemon on :3000. Port isolation +
      DUCKBRAIN_URL made the documented loop pass in 1s.
    
    Also verified and reported: AUG-036 and AUG-037 are FIXED in the current tree
    (bare option index resolves; ambiguity refused rc=1; dump --config shorthand
    parsed); AUG-038 still live (`--domain` accepts any string); `status` now measures
    199ms vs the 2.2s of AUG-047.
    
    What held up under real use: `dump --config` named a contradiction against the
    record unprompted; `toggle` refused an ambiguous token by name and wrote nothing;
    `init --seed-domains` still reads the grid rather than copying it.
    
    Install leg PASSED (unlike run 4's explicit skip): substrate 142s + documented
    loop 1s on a bare agent (bunker-las-03, agent d1a530b6, destroyed).
    
    Evidence: docs/dogfood/2026-09-24-real-drill-integration.md (report),
    docs/dogfood/diagnostics.md (root causes + failure signatures),
    skills/auger-usage/SKILL.md (pitfalls for the next agent),
    .coding-hermes/dogfood-log.md (verdict + install_seconds).
