e`\n- the stored question row records WHICH model proposed and WHICH scored (provenance,\n  so a weak proposal is visible rather than blamed on JEV)\n- the budget ceiling from AUG-001 still binds the batch size\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- `ask` can return more than one candidate question, each with its provenance\n- an already-answered candidate is dropped by the JEV gate, not by string match\n- the run ceiling still holds and still emits the budget-thin marker\n- the current single-subject path still works when the generator is unavailable\n  (degrades, never refuses)\n\nCOST NOTE: `ask` today costs 3.36e-05 (JEV only). A generator adds one\nlarge-context model call per ask; the row must state the measured delta before\nlanding, not after.", "status": "pending", "title": "DESIGN 4.3 open decision: `ask` takes JEV's single `next_subject` choice \u2014 split generation from judgement so a large-context model proposes candidate questions and JEV dedupes/ranks/scores them", "updated_at": "2026-09-23T23:26:02.631396+00:00"}
 {"attempts": 0, "blocks": [], "capability_tags": ["+decision", "+ops"], "ci_result": null, "commit_hash": null, "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-09-23T23:26:02.637825+00:00", "depends_on": [], "detail": {"fingerprint": "22c97e1afafa701005b665f79616747d61b10b30e8d3c7bd4b220408d3e5c114"}, "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": null, "guard_result": null, "id": "AUG-053", "perpetual": null, "priority": "P3", "reasoning": "WHY (same sweep as AUG-052 \u2014 the decision currently lives only in a doc)\n\ndocs/DESIGN.md section 4, open decision 2: \"v0.1 is Python (stdlib only) so the loop\ncould be proven the same day. The fleet convention for durable daemons is a single Go\nbinary + systemd + a loopback port. Recommend: keep Python while the shape is moving,\nport once the verbs stop changing.\"\n\nMeasured facts that make this decidable rather than theoretical:\n- auger is 4,200+ lines of stdlib-only Python and `auger` is NOT on PATH; it runs as\n  `python3 auger.py` from the clone.\n- 13 verbs and 14 tables are now stable; several verbs are still moving (AUG-019\n  write paths, AUG-029 bundles, AUG-005 export).\n- everything auger needs at runtime is a CLI invocation, not a resident process \u2014\n  so the systemd/daemon argument applies only if the feedback loop is ever run\n  unattended (which is exactly the AUG-001 governor question).\n\nDELIVERABLE: a recorded decision with its TRIGGER, not a code change. Either\n(a) stay Python \u2014 and say what would force the port, or (b) scope the port as its own\nrow with the verbs frozen and the substrate HTTP API as the boundary.\nDo NOT start a port before the verb surface stops changing; DESIGN says so explicitly.\n\nACCEPTANCE CRITERIA\n- the decision and its trigger condition are on the board (this row closes with the\n  decision text, not a commit)\n- if the answer is \"port\", a follow-up row exists naming the frozen verb list\n- no code change ships under this row", "status": "pending", "title": "DESIGN 4.2 open